\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord of Life and King of Glory,
\par Who didst deign a child to be,
\par Cradled on a mother's bosom,
\par Throned upon a mother's knee:
\par For the children Thou hast given
\par We must answer unto Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Since the day the blessed mother
\par Thee, the world's Redeemer, bore,
\par Thou hast crowned us with an honour
\par Women never knew before;
\par And, that we may  bear it meetly,
\par We must seek Thine aid the more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Grant us, then, pure hearts and patient,
\par That, in all we do or say,
\par Little souls our deeds may copy,
\par And be never led astray;
\par Little feet our steps may follow
\par In a safe and narrow way.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. When our growing sons and daughters
\par Look on life with eager eyes,
\par Grant us then a deeper insight,
\par And new powers of sacrifice:
\par Hope to trust them, faith to guide them,
\par Love that nothing good denies.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. May we keep our holy calling
\par Stainless in its fair renown,
\par That, when all the work is over,
\par And we lay the burden down,
\par Then the children Thou  hast given
\par Still may be our joy and crown.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

